# Flutter — Bottom Navigation

## 1. What is Bottom Navigation?

Bottom navigation lets the user switch between the **main sections of an app**.

Example:

```text
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│                             │
│        Screen content       │
│                             │
├─────────────────────────────┤
│  🏠       🔍       👤       │
│ Home    Search    Profile   │
└─────────────────────────────┘
```

Common sections:

* Home
* Search
* Favorites
* Cart
* Profile

---

## 2. Modern Flutter: NavigationBar

The important widget to learn is:

```dart
NavigationBar
```

It is placed inside:

```dart
Scaffold(
  bottomNavigationBar: NavigationBar(...)
)
```

---

## 3. Basic Example

```dart
int selectedIndex = 0;

Scaffold(
  body: Center(
    child: Text("Screen $selectedIndex"),
  ),

  bottomNavigationBar: NavigationBar(
    selectedIndex: selectedIndex,

    onDestinationSelected: (index) {
      setState(() {
        selectedIndex = index;
      });
    },

    destinations: [
      NavigationDestination(
        icon: Icon(Icons.home),
        label: "Home",
      ),

      NavigationDestination(
        icon: Icon(Icons.search),
        label: "Search",
      ),

      NavigationDestination(
        icon: Icon(Icons.person),
        label: "Profile",
      ),
    ],
  ),
)
```

---

## 4. How `selectedIndex` works

Suppose:

```text
0 → Home
1 → Search
2 → Profile
```

Initially:

```dart
int selectedIndex = 0;
```

So Home is selected.

When the user taps Search:

```dart
onDestinationSelected: (index) {
  setState(() {
    selectedIndex = index;
  });
}
```

`index` becomes `1`.

Flutter rebuilds the UI and Search becomes selected.

---

## 5. Showing Different Screens

Create your screens:

```dart
final screens = [
  HomeScreen(),
  SearchScreen(),
  ProfileScreen(),
];
```

Then:

```dart
body: screens[selectedIndex],
```

So:

```text
selectedIndex = 0
       ↓
HomeScreen

selectedIndex = 1
       ↓
SearchScreen

selectedIndex = 2
       ↓
ProfileScreen
```

---

## 6. Complete Example

```dart
int selectedIndex = 0;

final screens = [
  HomeScreen(),
  SearchScreen(),
  ProfileScreen(),
];

Scaffold(
  body: screens[selectedIndex],

  bottomNavigationBar: NavigationBar(
    selectedIndex: selectedIndex,

    onDestinationSelected: (index) {
      setState(() {
        selectedIndex = index;
      });
    },

    destinations: [
      NavigationDestination(
        icon: Icon(Icons.home_outlined),
        selectedIcon: Icon(Icons.home),
        label: "Home",
      ),

      NavigationDestination(
        icon: Icon(Icons.search_outlined),
        selectedIcon: Icon(Icons.search),
        label: "Search",
      ),

      NavigationDestination(
        icon: Icon(Icons.person_outline),
        selectedIcon: Icon(Icons.person),
        label: "Profile",
      ),
    ],
  ),
)
```

---

## 7. Important properties

### `selectedIndex`

Which item is currently selected.

```dart
selectedIndex: selectedIndex
```

### `onDestinationSelected`

Runs when the user taps an item.

```dart
onDestinationSelected: (index) {
  setState(() {
    selectedIndex = index;
  });
}
```

### `destinations`

Contains the navigation items.

```dart
destinations: [
  NavigationDestination(...),
  NavigationDestination(...),
]
```

---

## 8. Drawer vs Bottom Navigation

```text
Drawer
→ Side menu
→ Many options
→ Settings, About, Logout, etc.

Bottom Navigation
→ Main app sections
→ Home, Search, Profile, etc.
```

They can also be used **together** in the same application.
